  "content": {
    "id": "p20-q2-root",
    "type": "question",
    "label": "2",
    "prompt": "The base $a$ is positive and not equal to 1.\n\nSimplify $\\log_a(a^2+a)-\\log_a(a+1)$.",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [],
    "answer": {
      "short": "$1$",
      "worked": "Using the quotient law and $a^2+a=a(a+1)$:\n\n$$\\begin{align*}\\log_a(a^2+a)-\\log_a(a+1)&=\\log_a\\left(\\frac{a^2+a}{a+1}\\right)\\\\\\log_a(a^2+a)-\\log_a(a+1)&=\\log_a\\left(\\frac{a(a+1)}{a+1}\\right)\\\\\\log_a(a^2+a)-\\log_a(a+1)&=\\log_a a\\\\\\log_a(a^2+a)-\\log_a(a+1)&=1\\end{align*}$$",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
    "answerSpaceMm": 40
  },
